# round 120 (w137): betaxanthin. bxdel: the control backbone on deletion-only cell graphs (--deletion-only-graph), so the cassette's ARO4-K229L and ARO7-G141S alleles stay in every graph and out of the pooled perturbed-gene set; paired against w134_bxctx, the same backbone with the two allele nodes removed. bxgpr: the six gene-protein-reaction redundancy columns of every GEM gene (ess_solve_encodings_GEM_gpronly.npz) beside the YPD ratio, zero-init affine, the 028 round-77 columns carried to the target; paired against w134_bxctx.
